            <ArticleTitle>VDT work duration and musculoskeletal discomfort.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Musculoskeletal discomfort, work position, and job stress factors were compared in government office workers grouped according to whether they used video display terminals more or less than 4 hours per day. The results of this study suggest that limits on VDT use to less than 4 hours per day do not necessarily protect against health problems. The occupational health nurse's role in preventive measures useful for alleviating the musculoskeletal health problems of office work are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
